{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/93077-unchained-and-other-demons","id":93077,"title":"Unchained and other demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-17T16:59:35-07:00","id":93077,"title":"Unchained and other demons","content":"There are of course plenty of other things called demons in the WoD at large, and the core book suggests that they interact sometimes- especially the mention of children of Unchained and a mortal looking for a &quot;true&quot; hell. How would you use characters that more closely resemble classical demons, like inhabitants of the Inferno, the imps summoned by Lucifuge hunters, beings summoned by magi from Pandemonium, malevolent Lilithim and so on, in a Demon the Descent game? How would they interact with the Unchained?<br /> <br /> Personally, running with the idea from the core book that angels are portrayed positively in art and literature due to the machinations of the God-Machine to make its job easier, I like the thought that Unchained are the 'real' demons (in a Demon game anyway) and the GM might have implanted false memories of falling from grace in the minds of the infernal creatures that are seen more typically as demons in order to make its rebellious servants' lives more difficult by association. Keeping with the Matrix/'behind the curtain of reality' feel, traditional demons are less 'real' than the Unchained- a legitimate threat in some cases, but not fully realized creatures in the same way, more like a very complex simulacrum that behaves in strange ways when Unchained go outside their usual parameters. The bit from How An Angel Dies with the cryptid that happens to resemble a demon from the Lesser Key of Solomon is a great example of what I imagine, it breathes fire and wreaks havoc like a proper hellbeast, but it isn't <i>really</i> what it appears to be. I could imagine an Exploit that lets you command or summon more traditional demons by giving your Cover the 'aura' of a being they are programmed to obey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:38:23-07:00","id":93438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/93077-unchained-and-other-demons#post93077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are of course plenty of other things called demons in the WoD at large, and the core book suggests that they interact sometimes- especially the mention of children of Unchained and a mortal looking for a &quot;true&quot; hell. How would you use characters that more closely resemble classical demons, like inhabitants of the Inferno, the imps summoned by Lucifuge hunters, beings summoned by magi from Pandemonium, malevolent Lilithim and so on, in a Demon the Descent game? How would they interact with the Unchained?</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) Unchained ARE classical demons. They're fallen angels, and that's what Christianity classically calls demons.<br /> <br /> 2) They would interact in the same exact way any other splat would be interacting with the Unchained, pretty much. They'd look at them, try and decide if, hey, can we use these guys in a war against God? Or will they be a hinderance? Individuals matter. Unchained deal with some rather unsavory things in order to accomplish their goals - human trafficking for one. Drug and gun smuggling. Corporate sabotage? &quot;Terrorist&quot; attacks? Pretty much any criminal activity? The DtD demons are part of in some way. <br /> <br /> So, if the Unchained thought they could get the power to make their own Hell, or destroy God, or the like by tapping into the power of the Inferno, they probably would do it. Its very easy for them to end up selling their morals down the drain very quickly. Its a lot like Breaking Bad. Start off doing bad things for the right reason... and then end up just doing bad things period. <br /> <br /> But there's not going to be some instant recognition or the like, if that's what you're asking. Goetic demons have nothing in common with maeljin, who have nothing in common with strix, who have nothing to do with evil ghosts. The same with DtD - they really don't have anything to do with each other, no more than they have to do with werewolves or vampires. Any interaction is going to be on a case-by-case basis, and depends on the views and attitudes of the individuals in question, how they actually meet, which will flavor everything. There's no universal stance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, running with the idea from the core book that angels are portrayed positively in art and literature due to the machinations of the God-Machine to make its job easier, I like the thought that Unchained are the 'real' demons (in a Demon game anyway) and the GM might have implanted false memories of falling from grace in the minds of the infernal creatures that are seen more typically as demons in order to make its rebellious servants' lives more difficult by association. Keeping with the Matrix/'behind the curtain of reality' feel, traditional demons are less 'real' than the Unchained- a legitimate threat in some cases, but not fully realized creatures in the same way, more like a very complex simulacrum that behaves in strange ways when Unchained go outside their usual parameters. The bit from How An Angel Dies with the cryptid that happens to resemble a demon from the Lesser Key of Solomon is a great example of what I imagine, it breathes fire and wreaks havoc like a proper hellbeast, but it isn't <i>really</i> what it appears to be. I could imagine an Exploit that lets you command or summon more traditional demons by giving your Cover the 'aura' of a being they are programmed to obey. </div> </div> </div> Not sure what you're really aiming for here. Do you just want something summon-able? <br /> <br /> Occult Matrix and Interfaces are just strange words for &quot;ritual spell&quot; and &quot;spell components.&quot; There's no reason that a ritual to summon one of the Unchained demons couldn't be used, especially to call up a demon that HAS established its own Hell. Or, in an ironic twist, summon an angel.<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally have nothing against the Unchained being summon-able. Its probably something that they generally despise - the vast majority of them, now free from the God Machine's control, don't like being pulled around by another being. Likewise, its probably a disaster on their Cover, calling for compromise checks. Between being pulled around by some upstart, and the Cover checks, I'd image most Unchained would be pretty mad / scared, and want to put this threat to their freedom and safety down (thus danger to summoner). <br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if methods of a mortal calling a demon wouldn't make its way into other books. Not really worth a mention in the core book, I think - what demon would want to call up another demon in that way? That's pretty dangerous and a good way to start things on a bad foot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for infernal demons having memories implanted of a fall... who's to say that any of them are telling the truth? After how much they get twisted, how much of any of their memories are anything close to real? Or maybe some Unchained actually did establish a Hell in the Inferno - the one from Babylon is Fallen was happy to go back to the Inferno, which isn't something Inferno demons would ever agree to -they generally hate being in the Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}